From c505769802e9a920d3f4b987a2b39371c78af74f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit <dev@local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 06:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hardening 0.2.1: fix CSV injection bypass, non-deterministic
 output, action code 10, non-atomic writes

Security:
- sanitize_csv_field decided escaping on the raw first byte. Spreadsheet
  clients strip leading whitespace and normalise full-width punctuation before
  evaluating a cell, so tab/NBSP-prefixed payloads and full-width triggers were
  written unescaped; the DDE pipe was not a trigger at all. Escaping now keys
  on the first significant character, and the numeric bypass requires a finite
  value matching a strict decimal pattern.

Fixed:
- Column detection iterated a set of header names. With randomised string
  hashing, targets sharing a pattern bound to different source columns between
  runs, producing different output for identical input and silently dropping
  rows on some seeds.
- Action code 10 (Constant, FW 5.2.02+) was rewritten to 1, altering device
  behaviour. It is now preserved.
- write_output_csv streamed directly onto the destination, so a mid-run failure
  truncated an existing production definition. Output is staged via mkstemp and
  moved into place with os.replace.

Added:
- Post-generation validation for run (--no-validate), --force overwrite guard,
  --lenient validate, -q/--quiet, --version, verbosity flags on either side of
  the sub-command, actionable diagnostics.
- 26 regression tests (77 -> 103).

Changed:
- ~1.46x throughput via precompiled specificity-ordered synonym table behind
  lru_cache, memoised address/width lookups, frozenset action sets, O(K) column
  detection. Parity verified over 600k random tokens with zero divergence.
